ies-have-programs-that-allow-students-to-live-in-retirement-communities" /><summary type="html">Universities are offering students an alternative to the typical on-campus and off-campus living options: living alongside seniors in a retirement community.</summary></entry><entry><title>It's Election Day. Here's what to watch</title><id>https://www.npr.org/2026/11/03/nx-s1-6027772/its-election-day-heres-what-to-watch</id><updated>2026-11-03T21:54:02Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T20:52:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.npr.org/2026/11/03/nx-s1-6027772/its-election-day-heres-what-to-watch--b02fca6ede1e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.npr.org/2026/11/03/nx-s1-6027772/its-election-day-heres-what-to-watch" /><summary type="html">NPR's senior political correspondents break down what they're watching on Election Day across the country.</summary></entry><entry><title>Chicago entrepreneur turns empty downtown office space into vertical gardens</title><id>https://www.npr.org/2026/11/03/nx-s1-5944524-e1/chicago-entrepreneur-turns-empty-downtown-office-space-into-vertical-gardens</id><updated>2026-11-03T21:53:47Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T20:52:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.npr.org/2026/11/03/nx-s1-5944524-e1/chicago-entrepreneur-turns-empty-downtown-office-space-into-vertical-gardens--ecd6728abcbc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.npr.org/2026/11/03/nx-s1-5944524-e1/chicago-entrepreneur-turns-empty-downtown-office-space-into-vertical-gardens" /><summary type="html">The pandemic changed how and where the world works, leaving behind a lot of empty office space. One entrepreneur is starting to plant the seeds of a partial solution.</summary></entry><entry><title>Republican Rep. Don Bacon on what a potential blue wave could mean for the GOP</title><id>https://www.npr.org/2026/11/03/nx-s1-6027729/republican-rep-don-bacon-on-what-a-potential-blue-wave-could-mean-for-the-gop</id><updated>2026-11-03T21:53:41Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T20:52:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.npr.org/2026/11/03/nx-s1-6027729/republican-rep-don-bacon-on-what-a-potential-blue-wave-could-mean-for-the-gop--98e64ab1305c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.npr.org/2026/11/03/nx-s1-6027729/republican-rep-don-bacon-on-what-a-potential-blue-wave-could-mean-for-the-gop" /><summary type="html">NPR's Ailsa Chang talks with Republican Congressman Don Bacon of Nebraska about what a Blue Wave would mean for Republicans.</summary></entry><entry><title>How voting is going and where we go from here</title><id>https://www.npr.org/2026/11/03/nx-s1-6026635/how-voting-is-going-and-where-we-go-from-here</id><updated>2026-11-03T21:54:05Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T20:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.npr.org/2026/11/03/nx-s1-6026635/how-voting-is-going-and-where-we-go-from-here--b3657a3b1a56.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.npr.org/2026/11/03/nx-s1-6026635/how-voting-is-going-and-where-we-go-from-here" /><summary type="html">A look at how voting is going on Election Day, and what states to pay attention to as vote-counting begins.</summary></entry><entry><title>Georgia Voters go to the polls to elect a new governor and decide fate of Sen. Ossoff</title><id>https://www.npr.org/2026/11/03/nx-s1-6026383/georgia-voters-go-to-the-polls-to-elect-a-new-governor-and-decide-fate-of-sen-ossoff</id><updated>2026-11-03T21:54:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T20:51:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.npr.org/2026/11/03/nx-s1-6026383/georgia-voters-go-to-the-polls-to-elect-a-new-governor-and-decide-fate-of-sen-ossoff--e618262cc473.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.npr.org/2026/11/03/nx-s1-6026383/georgia-voters-go-to-the-polls-to-elect-a-new-governor-and-decide-fate-of-sen-ossoff" /><summary type="html">We check in on a G